# Rules that apply to the whole repo. Anything true of only one of the three
# folders belongs in that folder's own .gitignore, where its paths stay
# relative to the thing they describe — see sporra-webserver/.gitignore for
# the database and the map data, and the two app folders for Xcode's leavings.

# Local Claude Code settings (personal permissions); .claude/ itself is shared
.claude/settings.local.json

# The nightly worktree lives here. It is a second checkout of this same repo,
# so committing it would commit the repo into itself.
.claude/worktrees/

# iCloud conflict copies ("main 2.js") — this project sits under a synced
# ~/Documents, and a conflicted duplicate of a source file is never wanted.
* [0-9].*

# Editor backups ("SettingsView~.swift", "SettingsView.swift~"), which are the
# same hazard as the line above and worse inside the two app folders. Both Xcode
# projects use file-system synchronised groups, so **every** .swift file in the
# folder is compiled whether anything references it or not — a backup left
# beside its original is a second `struct SettingsView`, and the build fails
# with "Invalid redeclaration" in a file nobody edited and git never mentioned.
*~
*~.*

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
